<title>USA: Union 1,125 MW Mo. plant resumes output.</title>
<headline>Union 1,125 MW Mo. plant resumes output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Electric Co's 1,125 megawatt Callaway nuclear power plant has resumed electricity production following a scheduled outage which began Oct 12, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The plant was operating at 30 percent power and was holding at that level for testing as of early Wednesday, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The Fulton, Mo., plant was shut Oct 12 for scheduled refueling and maintenance, and began startup on Tuesday, returning to production about a week ahead of the original schedule.</p>
<p>--Chris Reese, New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
